\end{equation}

and that $K_{1-\alpha}(\mathrm{corr}(\Gamma_n)) = K_{1-\alpha}(\mathrm{corr}(\mathbb{V}_n(r_n))) > 0$. It now follows from Theorem \ref{thm:cons} (the special case with $\hat{K}_n = K_{1-\alpha}(\mathrm{corr}(\Gamma_n))$, that for any (measurable) model selection procedure $\hat{\mathbb{M}}_n$ it holds that

\begin{equation}
