\circ X_n^{(2)} \sim N(0, \rho^*I_n)$, and hence the distribution of $Y_n := X_n^{(1)} + X_n^{(2)}$ is $Q_n(0, \rho^*)$. Let $\varepsilon > 0$ be fixed. From the previous display it follows that $\mathbb{Q}(|\hat{\sigma}^2_n(Y_n) - (1 + \rho^*)  | > \varepsilon )$ converges to $0$. Since the conditional distribution of $Y_n$ given $X_n^{(2)}$ is $Q_n(X_n^{(2)}, 0)$, it furthermore holds that

